{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-minus-layers-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:18:54.186Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"41994b285ec097a9b206ea828ca8262cdf6c75e52da447ce16dbf94d2c1e0fc0","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two QFL ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from *Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth* (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. At the Eau Claire yard, drivers checking in on the gatehouse kiosk tablets at Dock Doors 14–18 for the 04:00 shift weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through the gate with no manual fixes. The digest also had a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from *Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)* (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for firmware testing. The sheet has no date, so I can't tell when it was logged or whether it's still open.\n\nA few things to watch for in the weekly notes:\n- Moss's other two North digests (2025-09-14 and 2026-03-23) mention QFL but don't include any ticket numbers.\n- **#4409** and **#4412** in the Central handoffs digest belong to Marrow Fieldworks, not QFL. #4409 is easy to mix up with #4419.\n- I only checked Moss's notes that you have access to, the public team digests. Your #general and #help-it-ops channels have no messages yet. I didn't look in the QFL account's ticket system, so there may be tickets Moss never wrote down."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
